==Russian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ru|Вы||alternative capitalisation in formal writing}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ru|orv|вꙑ}}, from {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*vy}}, from {{inh|ru|ine-pro|*yúHs}}. Cognate with {{cog|sa|यूयम्}} and {{cog|en|you}}.

Use of Вы as a formal singular is attested in East Slavic literature from the 11th-16th century, under influence of Medieval Greek speech. It started becoming widespread in Russian society during the rule of {{w|Peter the Great}}, under French and German influence, and became ingrained by the 19th century.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-вы.ogg}}

===Pronoun===
{{head|ru|pronoun|cat2=personal pronouns}}

# [[you]] {{q|plural or formal singular}}
#* {{quote-book|ru|year=1869|author=w:ru:Лев Толстой<t:{{w|Leo Tolstoy}}>|title=w:ru:[[Война и мир]]|chapter=s:ru:[[Война_и_мир_(Толстой)/Том_2|Том 2, Часть четвёртая, VIII]]|location=|publisher=|newversion=English translation from|translator2=w:en:Aylmer and Louise Maude|title2=s:en:[[War and Peace (Tolstoy)/Book 7/Chapter 8|War and Peace]]|location2=Oxford|publisher2=Oxford University Press|year2=1922–1923|page2=|pageurl2=|text=Она́ упрека́ла себя́ за то, но не могла́ не ворча́ть, не придира́ться к Со́не, ча́сто без причи́ны остана́вливая её, называ́я её «'''вы'''», и «моя́ ми́лая».|t=Though she blamed herself for it, she could not refrain from grumbling at and worrying Sónya, often pulling her up without reason, addressing her stiffly as “my dear,” and using the '''formal “you”''' instead of the intimate “thou” in speaking to her.}}

====Usage notes====
The personal pronoun {{lang|ru|вы}} is comparable to French {{m|fr|vous}}, German {{m|de|Sie}}, Italian {{m|it|Voi}}, Spanish {{m|es|usted}}, Portuguese {{m|pt|vós}}, and is used not only in the plural sense, but also as the formal singular. The formal {{lang|ru|вы}} is appropriate with strangers, business contacts, neighbors, and friends. (The informal {{m|ru|ты}} should only be used with family and friends. Even then, a speaker may suddenly switch to {{lang|ru|вы}} in order to broach an especially serious topic, or to indicate displeasure or anger.) For more information, see [[Appendix:Russian pronouns]]

